  "description": "Val Cenis links the traditional villages of Lanslebourg, Lanslevillard, and Termignon in the Haute Maurienne valley. 125km of pistes rising to 2,800m. The signature run is L'Escargot \u2014 one of the longest green runs in Europe at 10km. First French resort to invest in an electric snow groomer (local hydroelectric power). First resort with 96% undeveloped land. 6-day pass gives 1 free day in 5 neighbouring resorts (350km total). 200km of cross-country. 4.5 million litres of milk produced locally for Beaufort cheese.",
